Let a track with no clips still receive live MIDI (note previews)

createNodeForAudioTrack builds the track's node from its clips, then wraps
it in a LiveMidiInjectingNode -- the node that AudioTrack::playGuideNote
ultimately delivers to. A track with nothing on the timeline produces no
node from its clips, so the wrap is skipped; only afterwards does the
function notice the track hosts a synth and make a SilentNode to feed it.

The result is a synth track that plays back fine once something is placed
on it, but silently swallows every guide note until then: injectLiveMidiMessage
finds no listener for the track and drops the message. In an app whose piano
roll previews notes as they are drawn, that reads as "previews work on some
generators and not others".

Moving the wrap after the stub-node block fixes it. A track that did produce
a clips node is unaffected: the wrap still happens in the same place relative
to the live-input and input-track summing below.

